Rewrite install-termux.sh or remove it

install-termux.sh cannot work as written and is unreachable from any make target:

- :10 clones a second copy of the repo into whatever the CWD happens to be, before its own
  `cd "$HOME"` on :13, discarding the checkout the user is running from.
- It never calls init.sh, so it links no configs at all. The single highest-value missing
  line is `bash "$DOTFILES/make/init.sh"`.
- It never sources make/modules/, so none of the shared helpers exist.
- It ends by installing termux-style, whose menu is interactive.
- bun is not packaged for Termux; `pkg install nodejs-lts` and skipping nvm is the
  equivalent.

init.sh itself does work correctly on Termux, verified in a container: 13 of 13 symlinks
valid. So install-init.sh now tells Termux users to run `bash make/init.sh` directly and
exits non-zero, instead of printing three /etc/os-release errors and exiting 0 having
installed nothing. That is a holding position, not a fix.

If real support is added, dispatch must invoke installers as `bash "$script"` rather than
relying on shebangs: /usr/bin/env does not exist under the Termux prefix, so
`#!/usr/bin/env bash` cannot be resolved by the kernel there.

Also relevant to any Termux work, all found during the audit:

- Go binaries look for /etc/ssl/certs, which does not exist under the Termux prefix, so
  they fail with "x509: certificate signed by unknown authority" even where curl to the
  same host works. The shared setup_go_tls helper points SSL_CERT_FILE at
  $PREFIX/etc/tls/cert.pem; krew, gh, kubectl, eksctl, k9s and kustomize all need it.
- /usr/local/bin is not on Termux's PATH, and can_root is true on a rooted device with
  tsu, so install_binary needed an explicit $PREFIX/bin branch.
- Six things upstream simply does not publish for Android and which are now recorded as
  unsupported rather than failed: the AWS CLI v2, the Azure CLI, gke-gcloud-auth-plugin,
  gh-dash, and (via dependencies with no Android wheel and no Rust compiler) llm and
  parllama.

The container image is termux/termux-docker:x86_64, so it is indicative only: no Android
permissions model, no termux-api, /system is a stub, and the x86_64 target triple differs
from a real aarch64 device.
